# tally 2.2.1 P30 (L §4.4 l.667 to l.671): an operation decides over an interval only what holds for every value
# the interval can hold; its ends stand for them only where it is monotone and gives a value everywhere between.
# B3: days_between(d1, w) / days_between(d0, w) > 100 is false on 03-10 and 03-12 and RUN-DIV on 03-11 (the
# divisor's interval holds 0), so the hole. tally 2.2 printed false from the ends.
=== b3_div.tally
model b3
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input w: date
input wl: date
input d0: date
input d1: date
input de: date
input n2: num
input n100: num
input m1: num
input mm: month
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) "c"
  wl = window(2026-01-01, 2027-06-01) "c"
  d0 = 2026-03-11 "c"
  d1 = 2026-03-01 "c"
  de = 2025-12-30 "c"
  n2 = 2 "c"
  n100 = 100 "c"
  m1 = -1 "c"
  mm = 2026-02 "c"
ask dvc: days_between(d1, w) / days_between(d0, w) > n100
ask dvc_a: days_between(d1, w) / days_between(d0, w) > n100 with w = 2026-03-10
ask dvc_b: days_between(d1, w) / days_between(d0, w) > n100 with w = 2026-03-11
ask dvc_c: days_between(d1, w) / days_between(d0, w) > n100 with w = 2026-03-12
=== expect
dvc: ?"date within window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) not precise enough for arithmetic" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
dvc_a: false
  pinned: w = 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-01-01
dvc_b: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  pinned: w = 2026-03-11
  cut 2026-01-01
dvc_c: false
  pinned: w = 2026-03-12
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input de is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input m1 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input mm is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n2 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input wl is read by nothing
